  "motion": {
    "frames": 120,
    "note": "menacing growling T-Rex (HOME stance: low forward-leaning body on bent legs, balanced by the tail; head low and thrust forward, eyes wide open and glaring, jaw held open in a snarl; shoulders hunched, arms held ready with claws spread). Driver: a growl pulse twice a loop (peaked, not a sway). The chest heaves just before it (BR), the body tenses down a little (DIP, translation only so the planted feet keep their angle), the neck thrusts (NG, NG2), the jaw snaps wider (JAW) with a fast rumble on jaw and head (RUM), shoulders hunch (SH), elbows and wrists cock (EB, WB) and the claws fan wider (CL), each a beat later. The blade and crest settle; the tail base lifts against the head thrust and the tip lashes in a small travelling wave. Feet planted flat (motion.plant on the ankles); no body sway or roll.",
